# Renvor site — build-context exclusions.
#
# This file decides what the Docker daemon is even allowed to see. It is a confidentiality
# boundary before it is a performance optimisation: anything listed here cannot be copied
# into an image by accident, including by a future `COPY . .` that someone adds without
# thinking about it.
#
# The runtime stage copies only the generated site, so most of this never reaches a shipped
# layer regardless. That is defence in depth, not a reason to relax the list.

# --- Dependencies and package-manager state ---
# Installed inside the builder from the committed lockfile. Copying a host tree in would
# defeat `--frozen-lockfile` and could carry platform-specific binaries for the wrong arch.
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Generated output and caches ---
# The image builds these itself. Copying a host build in would let the shipped site drift
# from the source that supposedly produced it — the same reason they are git-ignored.
build/
.docusaurus/
.cache-loader/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Validation output ---
# Produced by the accessibility and container checks. Evidence of a run, never an input.
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/
sbom/
inspection/
*.screenshot.png

# --- Version control ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --- Environment and credentials (never build, never ship) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials
credentials.*
secrets/
*.secret

# --- Editor, IDE, and local agent state ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.specify/
.remember/

# --- Operating-system artefacts ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs and temporary files ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
tmp/
*.tmp

# --- Container definition and documentation ---
# The build does not need to read its own Dockerfile. No Markdown is an input either: the
# Docusaurus preset runs with `docs: false` and `blog: false`, so the site is built from
# `src/` and `static/` alone.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md
